1. Software Requirements
1.1 Database & Contact Management

Design a database to store contact information with explicit consent.

Fields include: email ID, mobile/WhatsApp number, social media handles, and parent contact details wherever applicable.

Ability to upload contact data in bulk using Excel / CSV / PDF files.

1.2 Job & Internship Portal

Alumni, staff, and partners can post job or internship opportunities.

Interface similar to a timeline feed.

Ability to filter posts by year, month, and date.

Search functionality for students and alumni.

1.3 Events Module

A dedicated events page where institutions can publish upcoming events.

Alumni can view events relevant to their respective institutions.

1.4 Social Media Broadcasting

A unified marketing/broadcasting tool to push announcements to all social media channels.

Recommended as a common marketing module to integrate with other VPM applications.

1.5 User Roles

Admin

Student

Alumnus

Approver (specific to approving alumni-related content)

1.6 Placement Partners

Maintain a list of partner companies and placement collaborators.

2. Alumni Portal – Home Page

Display institution photo, name, logo, and location.

Multi-institution support.

3. User Views / Features
3.1 Student View (Read-only unless specified)

View events from their institution.

Access job & internship listings with search by date.

Personal profile page with:

Contact details

Social media links

WhatsApp number, etc.

3.2 Admin View

Add or edit individual alumnus profiles.

Bulk upload alumni data using Excel.

Search and filter alumni by batch (year, stream, department).

Upload and manage events.

Post job opportunities or internships.

Social media broadcast interface for cross-platform announcements.

3.3 Approver View

Read-only access plus approval rights.

All newly added jobs, internships, events, and announcements must be approved before going live.

4. Newsletter Module

A central space for achievements, news, and major updates across all VPM institutions.

Alumni should be able to post advertisements or promotional content.

Optional monetization model to be explored (subscription, paid promotion slots, etc.).

5. Global SPOCs (Alumni Connect)

Ability to nominate and highlight volunteer coordinators based on geography:

Country → State → District → City → Town

Search and filter SPOCs based on location and available data.
